# Coach speech (Vietnamese): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach calls himself "tôi" and the player
# "bạn", "we / let's" = "chúng ta" (glossary/vi.md); Vietnamese has no gender agreement, so nothing
# depends on the player's or the coach's gender.
# Forms from common.lang: a move number is "{n:moveno}" = "nước thứ 12" (spoken "nước thứ mười hai"),
# always after "ở" ("ở {n:moveno}") or standing alone inside a sentence. The program capitalises no
# number, so a line that starts with the move number says "Nước {n:ord}" ("Nước thứ 12", spoken "Nước
# thứ mười hai"). An accuracy is "{acc:percent}" = "85%" (spoken "... phần trăm"), also where English
# writes a bare {acc}; counts use count.* ("{n:piece}" = "3 quân", "{m:time}" = "2 lần",
# "{n:best_move}" = "5 nước đi tốt nhất", "{m:check}" = "2 nước chiếu").
# "Won {pts} points" is said as material: "giành được {pts:point} lực lượng" at every level ({pts} is a
# net gain, e.g. 4 for a queen won against a rook: never "a piece worth {pts}").
# "Good move" is "nước đi hay", never "nước đi tốt" (heard as a pawn move).
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level} (written to fit every sentence that inserts them):
#   appraisal.phase.*   bare lower-case nouns ("trung cuộc"): after "giai đoạn", "ở", "riêng", or
#                       starting a sentence (the program capitalises it).
#   appraisal.reason.*  a complement said right after "hòa", no comma ("Hòa do lặp lại thế cờ.").
#   theme.*             a verb phrase, no full stop, said after a colon or after "hãy tập".
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name of the coach page (coach.level.<n>.name, as events.lang
#                       says them) in quotes, always after "cấp độ": "cấp độ “Người mới chơi”".
# {opening:def} inside a sentence, {opening} when the name stands alone or after a label.
# Forcing moves are named by what they are ("các nước chiếu, bắt quân và đe dọa"): clearer for a
# player than a calque.

